# Patent Claim

**1.** An apparatus comprising:

a processor; and

a memory storing instructions that, when executed by the processor, cause the apparatus to:

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;maintain a plurality of federated areas, each federated area of the plurality of federated areas defining a logical boundary within which access to one or more resources is governed by a respective set of access control rules;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;register a plurality of devices, wherein each device of the plurality of devices is associated with at least one federated area of the plurality of federated areas;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;define an inheritance relationship between a first federated area and a second federated area of the plurality of federated areas, wherein the inheritance relationship causes at least a subset of the access control rules of the first federated area to be propagated to the second federated area;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;assign a priority value to each of a plurality of access control rules applicable to a given device of the plurality of devices, the plurality of access control rules including at least one inherited access control rule propagated via the inheritance relationship and at least one local access control rule defined within a federated area associated with the given device;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;receive, from the given device, a request to access a resource within a target federated area of the plurality of federated areas;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;determine a set of applicable access control rules for the request by aggregating the at least one inherited access control rule and the at least one local access control rule;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;resolve a conflict between two or more of the applicable access control rules based at least in part on the priority value assigned to each of the two or more applicable access control rules, so as to select a governing access control rule; and

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;grant or deny the request to access the resource in accordance with the governing access control rule.

---

**Suggested dependent claims** you may wish to add:

- **2.** The apparatus of claim 1, wherein resolving the conflict comprises selecting, as the governing access control rule, the applicable access control rule having a highest priority value.

- **3.** The apparatus of claim 1, wherein the inheritance relationship is hierarchical such that the second federated area is a child of the first federated area, and wherein a local access control rule of the child overrides an inherited access control rule of the same subject matter when the local access control rule has a higher priority value.

- **4.** The apparatus of claim 1, wherein the instructions further cause the apparatus to log each grant or denial of access in an audit record associated with the target federated area.

- **5.** The apparatus of claim 1, wherein at least one of the plurality of devices is concurrently associated with two or more federated areas having differing sets of access control rules.

*Note: This is a sample drafted for illustrative purposes. Claim scope, terminology, and structure should be reviewed and tailored by a registered patent attorney or agent in view of your specific invention and relevant prior art.*
